  heading: "The William Reynolds Fine Art Collection"
  paragraphs:
    - "Our next special event in Gary Germer's estate event room is the incredible fine art collection of William Reynolds. A two-time Oscar winning film editor for The Sting & Sound of Music and an avid art collector has amassed a number of masterpieces before his passing. Now you get to own a piece of history and shop Mr. Reynolds' collection from some of the biggest names in art, such as Matisse and Picasso. This is a special one weekend event in our Vault Showroom Gallery showcasing over 50 works of art from a variety styles from European and Pacific Northwest artists. You might even get a chance to see the actual Oscar award for his Sound of Music win!"
    - "Artists represented are: Henri Matisse, Pablo Picasso, George Braque, Camille Pissaro, Paul Cezanne, George Rouault, Maurice Savin, Frantz Piking, Bernard Buffet, Francis Smith, Massimo Campigli, Antonio Clave, Alberto Giacomeo, Bisiaux, Keiko Minami, Augustin Ubeda, Jacques Bartoli, Edgar Degas, Charles Henney, David McCosh, Albert Bierstadt, Sally Haley, Albert Patecky, Carol Griggs, Dee Boyles, Jan Van Empel, Carl Clemens Moritz, Jules Dahlager, Walter Thompson, Shirley Gittelsohn, Jack McLarty."
    - "Follow us on our socials for sneak peaks and teasers!"
